a1=$.c==="en"
a2=a1?"Use inspection like the best":"Quan s\xe1t 15 gi\xe2y nh\u01b0 ng\u01b0\u1eddi gi\u1ecfi"
a3=a1?"Plan the whole cross \u2013 and, when you can, the first pair too.":"L\xean k\u1ebf ho\u1ea1ch c\u1ea3 d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng \u2013 v\xe0 n\u1ebfu \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c, c\u1ea3 c\u1eb7p \u0111\u1ea7u ti\xean."
r=a1?"Fast solvers don't just find the cross during the 15 s inspection: they memorise the whole cross sequence before starting the timer, then execute it without looking back.":"Ng\u01b0\u1eddi gi\u1ea3i nhanh kh\xf4ng ch\u1ec9 t\xecm d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng trong 15 gi\xe2y quan s\xe1t: h\u1ecd thu\u1ed9c l\xf2ng c\u1ea3 chu\u1ed7i b\u01b0\u1edbc d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng tr\u01b0\u1edbc khi b\u1ea5m gi\u1edd, r\u1ed3i gi\u1ea3i kh\xf4ng c\u1ea7n nh\xecn l\u1ea1i."
q=a1?"Short crosses: almost every cross can be done in 8 moves or fewer. Practise until you usually find 6\u20137 move solutions.":"D\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng ng\u1eafn: h\u1ea7u h\u1ebft d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng l\xe0m \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c trong 8 b\u01b0\u1edbc tr\u1edf xu\u1ed1ng. Luy\u1ec7n t\u1edbi khi b\u1ea1n th\u01b0\u1eddng xuy\xean t\xecm ra l\u1eddi gi\u1ea3i 6\u20137 b\u01b0\u1edbc."
p=a1?"The next step is the X-cross: the cross plus one F2L pair. At first, just notice when a pair is already close to its slot.":"B\u01b0\u1edbc ti\u1ebfp theo l\xe0 X-cross: d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng c\u1ed9ng lu\xf4n m\u1ed9t c\u1eb7p F2L. Ban \u0111\u1ea7u ch\u1ec9 c\u1ea7n nh\u1eadn ra khi n\xe0o c\u1eb7p \u0111\xe3 n\u1eb1m s\u1eb5n g\u1ea7n ch\u1ed7."
r=A.a([r,q,p,a1?"Drill: Cross practice (compare with the shortest solution), then X-cross mode and blindfolded mode.":"B\xe0i t\u1eadp: Luy\u1ec7n d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng (so v\u1edbi l\u1eddi gi\u1ea3i ng\u1eafn nh\u1ea5t), r\u1ed3i ch\u1ebf \u0111\u1ed9 X-cross v\xe0 ch\u1ebf \u0111\u1ed9 b\u1ecbt m\u1eaft."],s)
a1=$.c==="en"
q=a1?"Colour neutrality":"M\xe0u linh ho\u1ea1t"
p=a1?"Pick the easiest cross colour for each scramble instead of always white.":"Ch\u1ecdn m\xe0u d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng d\u1ec5 nh\u1ea5t c\u1ee7a m\u1ed7i chu\u1ed7i x\xe1o thay v\xec lu\xf4n l\xe0 m\xe0u tr\u1eafng."
o=a1?"Many of the world's fastest solvers can start on any colour: during inspection they compare a few colours and pick the one needing the fewest moves.":"Nhi\u1ec1u ng\u01b0\u1eddi gi\u1ea3i nhanh nh\u1ea5t th\u1ebf gi\u1edbi l\xe0m d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng \u1edf b\u1ea5t k\u1ef3 m\xe0u n\xe0o: trong 15 gi\xe2y quan s\xe1t h\u1ecd so v\xe0i m\xe0u v\xe0 ch\u1ecdn m\xe0u c\u1ea7n \xedt b\u01b0\u1edbc nh\u1ea5t."
n=a1?"Start with two opposite colours (white/yellow): your grip hardly changes and OLL/PLL recognition only swaps the top colour.":"B\u1eaft \u0111\u1ea7u b\u1eb1ng hai m\xe0u \u0111\u1ed1i nhau (tr\u1eafng/v\xe0ng): c\xe1ch c\u1ea7m g\u1ea7n nh\u01b0 kh\xf4ng \u0111\u1ed5i, nh\u1eadn d\u1ea1ng OLL/PLL ch\u1ec9 \u0111\u1ed5i m\xe0u m\u1eb7t tr\xean."
m=a1?"Switching colours slows F2L recognition at first \u2013 accept a few slower weeks for a long-term gain.":"\u0110\u1ed5i m\xe0u l\xe0m ch\u1eadm nh\u1eadn d\u1ea1ng F2L l\xfac \u0111\u1ea7u \u2013 ch\u1ea5p nh\u1eadn v\xe0i tu\u1ea7n ch\u1eadm h\u01a1n \u0111\u1ec3 v\u1ec1 l\xe2u d\xe0i nhanh h\u01a1n."
o=A.a([o,n,m,a1?'Drill: Cross practice in "Any colour" mode \u2013 the app shows which colour is shortest.':'B\xe0i t\u1eadp: Luy\u1ec7n d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng ch\u1ebf \u0111\u1ed9 "M\u1ecdi m\xe0u" \u2013 app cho bi\u1ebft m\xe0u n\xe0o ng\u1eafn nh\u1ea5t.'],s)
a1=$.c==="en"
n=a1?"F2L without pauses":"F2L kh\xf4ng d\u1eebng"
m=a1?"Most of a solve is F2L \u2013 cutting the pauses is the quickest way down.":"Ph\u1ea7n l\u1edbn th\u1eddi gian m\u1ed9t l\u01b0\u1ee3t n\u1eb1m \u1edf F2L \u2013 c\u1eaft c\xe1c l\u1ea7n d\u1eebng l\xe0 c\xe1ch nhanh nh\u1ea5t \u0111\u1ec3 xu\u1ed1ng th\u1eddi gian."
l=a1?"Look-ahead: while inserting one pair, your eyes are already finding the next. Top solvers have almost no gap between pairs.":"Nh\xecn tr\u01b0\u1edbc: trong l\xfac ch\xe8n c\u1eb7p n\xe0y, m\u1eaft \u0111\xe3 t\xecm c\u1eb7p ti\u1ebfp theo. Ng\u01b0\u1eddi gi\u1ecfi g\u1ea7n nh\u01b0 kh\xf4ng c\xf3 kho\u1ea3ng d\u1eebng gi\u1eefa c\xe1c c\u1eb7p."
k=a1?"Pick the easiest pair rather than a fixed order, and insert into back slots without rotating the cube.":"Ch\u1ecdn c\u1eb7p d\u1ec5 nh\u1ea5t, kh\xf4ng l\xe0m theo th\u1ee9 t\u1ef1 c\u1ed1 \u0111\u1ecbnh; ch\xe8n \u0111\u01b0\u1ee3c v\xe0o khe sau m\xe0 kh\xf4ng xoay c\u1ea3 cube."
j=a1?"Slow, steady turning beats fast and stop-start: practise to a slow beat until the pauses disappear, then speed up.":"Gi\u1ea3i ch\u1eadm kh\xf4ng d\u1eebng (slow turning) t\u1ed1t h\u01a1n nhanh m\xe0 kh\u1ef1ng: t\u1eadp theo nh\u1ecbp ch\u1eadm t\u1edbi khi kh\xf4ng c\xf2n d\u1eebng, r\u1ed3i m\u1edbi t\u0103ng t\u1ed1c."
l=A.a([l,k,j,a1?"Drills: Pick the easiest F2L pair, Predict the piece, Look-ahead to a metronome.":"B\xe0i t\u1eadp: Ch\u1ecdn c\u1eb7p F2L d\u1ec5 nh\u1ea5t, \u0110o\xe1n v\u1ecb tr\xed kh\u1ed1i, Luy\u1ec7n nh\xecn tr\u01b0\u1edbc theo nh\u1ecbp."],s)
a1=$.c==="en"
k=a1?"Last layer: from 2-look to 1-look and beyond":"T\u1ea7ng cu\u1ed1i: t\u1eeb 2-look t\u1edbi 1-look v\xe0 h\u01a1n n\u1eefa"
j=a1?"Know the algorithm path strong solvers take \u2013 and learn it in a sensible order.":"Bi\u1ebft l\u1ed9 tr\xecnh c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c c\u1ee7a ng\u01b0\u1eddi gi\u1ecfi \u2013 v\xe0 h\u1ecdc theo th\u1ee9 t\u1ef1 h\u1ee3p l\xfd."
i=a1?"The usual order: 2-look OLL/PLL \u2192 all 21 PLLs \u2192 all 57 OLLs. PLL first, because there are fewer and every solve uses one.":"Th\u1ee9 t\u1ef1 th\u01b0\u1eddng g\u1eb7p: 2-look OLL/PLL \u2192 \u0111\u1ee7 21 PLL \u2192 \u0111\u1ee7 57 OLL. H\u1ecdc PLL tr\u01b0\u1edbc v\xec \xedt h\u01a1n v\xe0 l\u01b0\u1ee3t n\xe0o c\u0169ng d\xf9ng."
h=a1?"Strong solvers also control edges at the last slot to make OLL easier, and learn sets such as COLL (a few dozen cases) or ZBLL (hundreds of cases) to often finish the last layer in one look.":"Ng\u01b0\u1eddi gi\u1ecfi c\xf2n ki\u1ec3m so\xe1t c\u1ea1nh \u1edf khe cu\u1ed1i \u0111\u1ec3 OLL d\u1ec5 h\u01a1n, v\xe0 h\u1ecdc th\xeam c\xe1c b\u1ed9 nh\u01b0 COLL (v\xe0i ch\u1ee5c tr\u01b0\u1eddng h\u1ee3p) hay ZBLL (h\xe0ng tr\u0103m tr\u01b0\u1eddng h\u1ee3p) \u0111\u1ec3 th\u01b0\u1eddng gi\u1ea3i t\u1ea7ng cu\u1ed1i trong m\u1ed9t l\u1ea7n."
g=a1?"They pick algorithms that suit their hands, not necessarily the shortest \u2013 and often keep one per angle to skip the U turn.":"H\u1ecd ch\u1ecdn c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c h\u1ee3p tay m\xecnh, kh\xf4ng nh\u1ea5t thi\u1ebft l\xe0 c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c ng\u1eafn nh\u1ea5t \u2013 v\xe0 th\u01b0\u1eddng c\xf3 c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c ri\xeang cho t\u1eebng g\xf3c \u0111\u1ec3 kh\u1ecfi xoay U tr\u01b0\u1edbc."
i=A.a([i,h,g,a1?"Drills: Full OLL/PLL path, Last slot to a yellow cross, Algorithm duel and per-angle algorithms (in the case sheet).":"B\xe0i t\u1eadp: L\u1ed9 tr\xecnh OLL/PLL \u0111\u1ea7y \u0111\u1ee7, Khe cu\u1ed1i ra d\u1ea5u c\u1ed9ng v\xe0ng, So t\xe0i c\xf4ng th\u1ee9c v\xe0 C\xf4ng th\u1ee9c theo g\xf3c (trong h\u1ed9p xem tr\u01b0\u1eddng h\u1ee3p)."],s)
